      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've classed the run as anomalous. Since growth started, exhaust O2 has gone up at every reading, from 1.7 to 25.3 ppm by 3240 s. Argon flow and temperature have stayed on setpoint, so they don't explain it. The most likely cause is air leaking in, probably through a seal, but I've left the cause as undetermined. This furnace has no tube pressure gauge, and growth needs one to confirm the atmosphere. That means I can't tell a seal leak from an exhaust problem or O2 sensor drift. There's no characterization of the sample yet, so there's no scientific result either way. My recommendation is to call a person to run a leak check or get a pressure reading and check the O2 sensor."
